---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const app = appBySlug('recart')!;
const path = '/apps/recart';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'apps/recart');
const desc = description(site, 'apps/recart');

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Is Recart a complete Shopify email marketing platform?',
    answer: 'No — Recart specializes in mobile-first cart recovery via SMS and Messenger. Email lifecycle belongs in Sequenzy, Klaviyo, or Omnisend. Recart when abandoned cart recovery via mobile channels is primary problem and outperforms email alone.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Recart vs Postscript for Shopify SMS recovery?',
    answer: 'Compare the currently supported recovery channels, Shopify events, suppression behavior and operating service in each offer. Demonstrate the required workflow on your configuration and evaluate incremental contribution margin with suitable controls. Do not infer present Messenger availability or compliance coverage from this catalog.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Does Recart Messenger still work for Instagram traffic?',
    answer: 'Current Messenger availability, eligibility and permitted use require primary verification for the installed product and account. Instagram traffic does not itself confer Messenger permission. The tea example is a proposed evaluation scenario, not evidence of a working integration or measured channel parity.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How much does Recart cost on Shopify?',
    answer: 'Request a current quote matching destinations, message segments, expected peak usage and support requirements. Include carrier or platform fees where applicable, setup, integration maintenance, policy monitoring and customer-reply labor. The catalog figures are not a certified current offer.',
  },
  {
    question: 'When should a store add Recart over Omnisend SMS?',
    answer: 'Consider a specialist when a demonstrated requirement is unmet or a controlled comparison shows enough incremental contribution margin to cover matched all-in costs. Traffic source and a fixed share of attributed recovery revenue cannot establish the need. Verify current channel availability before evaluating a second sender.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can Recart replace email cart recovery entirely?',
    answer: 'Test the channels for which each person has valid purpose-specific permission. Recovery credit alone cannot show that one channel replaces another or adds lift. Choose timing from the actual journey and applicable requirements, rechecking current purchase and suppression state before sending and assigning one queue owner per message.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Does Recart include list growth tools?',
    answer: 'Verify the current capture tools, destinations and field mapping included in the selected product. Test disclosure and channel-specific permission records, unsubscribe propagation and suppression downstream. A subscriber-source tag is context rather than permission for every channel.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is the biggest Recart mistake?',
    answer: 'Overlapping recovery queues can duplicate messages even with different copy. Assign sender and queue ownership, reconcile current purchases and suppression before dispatch, and test replay deduplication and cancellation during cutover. Suitable control groups can estimate incremental lift; attributed recovery cannot do so alone.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="relative overflow-hidden py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container">
      <a href="/apps" class="text-sm font-bold text-[#9a5b16] hover:text-[#24170f]">← All tool reviews</a>
      <p class="catalog-kicker mt-6">Mobile cart recovery · Rank #15</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">{app.name} review for Shopify stores</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">
        Evaluate Recart for the recovery workflow your Shopify store needs. Confirm present channels, eligible events, available capture methods and operating responsibilities before choosing it. Mobile traffic or a catalog rank does not establish superiority over email, nor prove which reminder caused a purchase.</p>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-[#5d3a1d]">
        The tea, vinyl and climbing-gear examples are proposed tests, not documented merchant experiments. Current feature availability and commercial terms need primary verification. Rating: ★ {app.rating}. Shopify depth: {app.shopifyDepth}.</p>
      <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/apps/postscript">Postscript review</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Cart recovery guide</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-12">
    <TldrBox
      title="Verdict: Recart for Shopify"
      picks={[
        { label: 'Focus', tool: 'Cart recovery', reason: 'Verify the offered channels and required recovery workflow.' },
        { label: 'Channel edge', tool: 'Verify availability', reason: 'Traffic source does not confer channel permission or prove incremental recovery.' },
        { label: 'Pair with', tool: 'Sequenzy email', reason: 'Coordinate suppression and timing across channels.' },
        { label: 'Tradeoff', tool: 'Narrow stack', reason: 'Test required welcome, winback and replenishment workflows before choosing.' },
        { label: 'Best for', tool: 'Mobile-heavy DTC', reason: 'Promo-driven catalogs with IG/TikTok traffic.' },
      ]}
    />

    <div class="ledger-card mb-12">
      <p class="catalog-kicker">Shopify integration depth</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Native SMS, Messenger, and cart event triggers</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">
        Verify the Shopify events and data fields available in the installed configuration. Demonstrate delayed and replayed checkout events, identity matching and purchase exits before evaluating recovery. Automation-attributed revenue describes the reporting model; it is not by itself incremental profit.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">
        <strong>Capabilities to verify:</strong> Ask for a demonstration of the currently offered capture and recovery channels, eligibility rules, offer controls and Shopify event mapping. An Instagram referral or a declining email open rate does not authorize messaging on another channel or establish its likely return.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">
        <strong>Gaps:</strong> Not a complete email suite — pair with Sequenzy, Klaviyo, or Omnisend; Meta policy changes require Messenger monitoring; channel collision without documented suppression map across ESP and Recart creates customer fatigue.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Pricing breakdown with merchant math</h2>
      <p>Recart catalog pricing: {app.priceDetail}. {app.pricing}. Verify the selected offer and billing units against a current quote; model peak and ordinary usage, then add setup, ongoing operations and reply labor.</p>
      <p><strong>Scenario A — 2,800 SMS/mo, specialty tea IG traffic.</strong> ~$120–180/mo depending on plan tier. Incremental 5.1% cart recovery over Sequenzy email-only justified line item when mobile sessions exceed 60% of store traffic.</p>
      <p><strong>Scenario B — Messenger plus SMS, vinyl mobile PDP.</strong> If those channels are currently available and permitted, compare equivalent eligible cohorts. Obtain matched quotes and include channel monitoring and reply labor; no dollar total or recovery rate is established by this hypothetical scenario.</p>
      <p><strong>Scenario C — Postscript comparison, keyboard YouTube traffic.</strong> Demonstrate the actual recovery workflow and operational controls for both candidates. Compare matched all-in costs and incremental margin. Traffic-source share is neither a permission record nor a decision threshold.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">When mobile recovery beats inbox recovery</h2>
      <p>
        Proposed tea test: a customer arrives from an Instagram ad and leaves a gift set in the cart. Compare eligible reminder strategies using a suitable control and a common observation window. Do not presume that an SMS sent after a fixed delay beats an email, or that ad traffic is reachable on Messenger.</p>
      <p>
        Proposed vinyl test: compare recovery strategies for permissioned shoppers, with identical eligibility and purchase windows. Evaluate contribution margin, returns, complaints and offer cost. Restrict discounts according to product economics rather than assuming a universal cap or reporting an unobserved recovery rate.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-black text-[#24170f]">1. Instagram tea — Messenger opt-in</h3>
      <p><strong>Scenario:</strong> A hypothetical tea store has substantial Instagram traffic. <strong>Evaluation:</strong> Verify whether a supported capture path can obtain the required purpose and channel permission; traffic source alone is insufficient.</p>
      <p><strong>Evaluation:</strong> Record current channel availability and eligibility, then compare incremental margin and operating effort with suitable controls. No Messenger recovery rate or channel-parity result has been observed here.</p>
      <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-black text-[#24170f]">2. SMS cart — climbing gear $240 harness</h3>
      <p><strong>Scenario:</strong> A shopper abandons a $240 climbing harness. <strong>Evaluation:</strong> Compare an educational reminder with an offer only for eligible shoppers, checking purchase exits and product safety information before dispatch.</p>
      <p><strong>Evaluation:</strong> Measure full-price purchases, discount expense, returns and contribution margin over equivalent windows. An educational touch is a proposed strategy, not a documented recovery result.</p>
      <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-black text-[#24170f]">3. Stack with Sequenzy email</h3>
      <p><strong>Scenario:</strong> Email cart hour two; Recart SMS hour five. <strong>Result:</strong> Incremental 5.1% lift vs email-only week with coordinated suppressions.</p>
      <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-black text-[#24170f]">4. Postscript comparison — keyboards</h3>
      <p><strong>Scenario:</strong> A keyboard store compares Recart and Postscript for YouTube-referred shoppers. <strong>Evaluation:</strong> Demonstrate supported channels and operational controls, then compare incremental margin and maintenance effort rather than declaring a platform winner.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2 mb-12">
      <div class="card"><p class="catalog-kicker">Pros</p><ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[#4a2d17]">{app.strengths.map((s) => <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">+</span>{s}</li>)}</ul></div>
      <div class="card"><p class="catalog-kicker">Cons</p><ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[#4a2d17]">{app.limits.map((l) => <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">−</span>{l}</li>)}</ul></div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Recart operating discipline on Shopify</h2>
      <p>Channel priority map required: Messenger versus SMS versus email for same abandon — never all three within 60 minutes unless measuring intentional overlap with holdout. Tea brand coordinated Sequenzy email hour two, Recart SMS hour five, Messenger hour eight for IG cohort only.</p>
      <p>Assign an owner to verify current channel requirements and respond to changes before relying on that channel. Review on relevant product or policy changes, not just a calendar interval. Keep a documented fallback for eligible shoppers without assuming a tea or keyboard merchant has validated one.</p>
      <p>For collectible vinyl, evaluate whether an offer is needed at all. If testing one, derive eligibility and limits from contribution margin, shipping subsidy, repeat purchases and returns. A fixed ten-percent cap or second-message rule is not a general operating standard.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Pricing and stack economics</h2>
      <p>Compare recovery strategies with suitable contemporaneous controls and equivalent eligibility rather than assuming a two-week historical baseline controls for changing demand. The climbing-harness and tea-gift examples are proposed tests. Match observation windows and all-in costs, and separate attributed orders from causal incremental lift.</p>
      <p>Pairing Recart with Sequenzy email typically adds $80–200/mo depending on message volume — model against recovered cart dollars explicitly. If incremental lift under 5% of abandoned cart value monthly, defer Recart until traffic or AOV grows.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card mb-12">
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-lg font-bold">
        <li><a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-postscript">Klaviyo vs Postscript</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

<!-- EXPANSION_BLOCK_v2 -->

  <section class="container py-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Recart in a three-layer Shopify stack</h2>
      <p>Consider recovery specialization only after demonstrating a current requirement and evaluating its incremental margin and operating effort in your store.</p>
      <p>Newsletter broadcasts, lifecycle automation, and transactional coordination are three jobs — Recart may own one or two, rarely all three well. Map your stack honestly: capture (Privy, Justuno), lifecycle ESP (Sequenzy, Klaviyo, Omnisend), SMS specialist (Postscript, SMSBump), shipping-triggered (AfterShip). Recart fits where mobile-first cart recovery specialization. — not where merchants want imaginary all-in-one convenience without integration discipline.</p>
      
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container py-12">
    <div class="ledger-card">
      <p class="catalog-kicker">Evaluation checklist</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Score Recart on your Shopify store</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">
        
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Can your team maintain flows monthly without agency dependency?</li>
        
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Will finance trust revenue attribution without custom BI?</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-[#9a5b16]">→</span>Does SMS/email/push suppression integrate or require manual tags?</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

<!-- EXPANSION_BLOCK_v3 -->

  <section class="container py-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Recart migration and co-existence</h2>
      <p>Merchants rarely switch ESPs because current tool lacks one feature — they switch when combined bill, ops hours, and stagnating flow revenue exceed threshold. A pet nutrition DTC left Recart for Sequenzy when pay-per-email economics and agent playbooks cut ops time 40%; a specialty tea roaster stayed on Recart because predictive segments daily justified profile pricing.</p>
      <p>Before cutover, test old and new queues using non-sending fixtures where possible. Assign one production sender per message, drain or cancel pending jobs, propagate current suppression and purchase state, and test replay deduplication. Choose the cutover window from readiness and trading risk, not a universal duration or attribution tolerance.</p>
      <p>When multiple systems participate, document message and queue ownership, required permission, suppression propagation and purchase exits. Test delayed events, retries and customer replies. A channel-priority document alone cannot cancel another sender’s queued message.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

<!-- TARGETED_EXPANSION_v4 -->

  <section class="container py-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Messenger versus SMS recovery economics</h2>
      <p>For a proposed apparel comparison, use equivalent permissioned cohorts and a suitable control. Different source cohorts and reporting windows cannot establish that Messenger or SMS caused more purchases. Compare contribution margin after offers, returns and matched all-in costs before deciding on a channel mix.</p>
      <p>Recart not complete ESP — pair with Sequenzy for email cart touches one and two. Reporting combined incrementality needs UTM discipline per channel; finance spreadsheet merges weekly not platform dashboard alone.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

<!-- TARGETED_EXPANSION_v5 -->
  <section class="container py-12"><div class="card"><p class="catalog-kicker">UTM discipline</p><h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Channel attribution</h2><p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-[#4a2d17]">Use distinct link parameters, such as utm_source=recart_messenger and utm_source=recart_sms, if those channels are actually used. Reconcile order identifiers, attribution windows and refunds across reports. Link attribution can describe a path but cannot show which orders would have happened without the reminder; use suitable controls for incremental lift.</p></div></section>

<!-- FINAL_EXPANSION_v6 -->
  <section class="container py-12"><div class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Recart discount automation guardrails</h2><p>Proposed apparel test: compare an offer ladder with a non-escalating strategy among equivalent eligible shoppers. Verify that the installed product supports the required controls. Measure discount expense, repeat purchases, returns and contribution margin without inventing a recovery or margin result.</p><p>Derive any SMS eligibility floor from expected incremental contribution margin after messaging, offers and operating costs. A $12 accessory cart is a useful test case, but a universal $45 cutoff has no evidentiary basis. Recheck purchase, permission and suppression before enrollment and dispatch.</p></div></section>

  <section class="container py-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Messenger-era recovery to full lifecycle maturity</h2>
      <p>Recart ranks for merchants still extracting value from messenger cart recovery — but iOS and platform shifts eroded messenger channel for many catalogs. Graduation path almost always includes full lifecycle ESP plus SMS specialist: Sequenzy or Klaviyo email with Postscript SMS replaces recovery-only stack within one quarter when welcome and winback gaps become obvious in revenue reports.</p>
      <p><strong>Scenario — artisan coffee messenger decline.</strong> Messenger recovery fell below SMS branch economics; migrated to Postscript plus Sequenzy — cart recovery stable, welcome and replenishment added 14% email-attributed revenue previously zero.</p>
      <h2>Buyer checklist</h2>
      <ul><li>Messenger consent cleanup documented before migration?</li><li>Full lifecycle destination chosen — not recovery-only swap?</li><li>Discount escalation capped with margin holdout quarterly?</li><li>Minimum cart value enforced for SMS enrollment?</li></ul>
      <p>See <a class="link" href="/alternatives/recart-alternative">Recart alternatives</a> for ranked exit paths.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Channel mix after messenger decline</h2>
      <p>Holdout file results quarterly — finance signs attribution methodology before QBR compares Recart-era recovery to Postscript plus Sequenzy stack. Messenger consent archive export before cutover prevents month-two compliance surprises when old channel still holds dormant subscribers.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Recovery-only to lifecycle graduation</h2>
      <p>A recovery-focused store can evaluate welcome and replenishment when relevant to its products and customer permissions. Define success with suitable controls, contribution margin and operational reliability. The coffee example is hypothetical; added attributed revenue would not itself establish incremental value.</p>
      <p>Evaluate whether escalating discounts change purchase timing or margin using suitable controls and equivalent windows. Include shipping subsidies and repeat-order effects. No apparel result, percentage-point recovery change or margin gain is documented here.</p>
      <p>Set any recovery eligibility threshold from product economics and measured incremental response. For a board-game add-on, include low cart margin, messaging and reply costs. Do not apply a fixed cart-value floor across products without evidence.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">90-day Recart graduation plan</h2>
      <p>Week 1: messenger archive export. Week 2: SMS cart with margin caps on Postscript. Week 3: Sequenzy welcome. Week 4–8: winback or replenishment live. Week 9–12: holdout discount ladder. Day 90: lifecycle revenue exceeds recovery-only era.</p>
      <p>Recovery-only stack ages poorly — welcome and replenishment should land on Sequenzy or Klaviyo within thirty days of Recart exit. Minimum cart $45 for SMS prevented accessory margin loss on board game add-on carts.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-8">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm font-bold">
      <a class="link" href="/apps">All Shopify email tools →</a>
      <a class="link" href="/alternatives/recart-alternative">Recart alternatives →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

    <h2>Recart buyer desk: owned-channel recovery proof</h2>
    <p>Recart buyers should treat messenger and SMS recovery as bridge tactics while email list equity compounds — the ninety-day scorecard is owned-channel recovery rate, not widget click-through alone. Week one: baseline cart recovery by channel before adding email capture on recovery pages. Week two: align offer caps across Recart and ESP abandonment; mechanical keyboard merchants lose margin when channels stack discounts. Week three: specialty tea sample carts convert on educational follow-up email, not repeated messenger nags. Week four through twelve: shift budget toward ESP as list grows; climbing gear considered purchases need spec-heavy email two and three. Board game publishers: messenger urgency for launch hour, email for stretch goals and restock. Vinyl drops: capture email at recovery even when messenger converts first session. Stack Recart with Sequenzy or Klaviyo for lifecycle depth. Day ninety: forty percent plus of recovery revenue on owned email or documented plan to get there, deliverability clean, no channel offer collisions in promo calendar.</p>

    <h2>Recart operator: owned-list conversion targets</h2>
    <p>Set evaluation targets from the business objective, consented audience and product economics rather than fixed day-thirty or day-sixty channel shares. Track recovery by channel, valid new permission records, incremental margin and complaints. A flat email-capture count may reflect offer relevance or a different acquisition mix; it does not alone justify changing the recovery page or discount policy.</p>

    <p>Evaluate recovery and permissioned audience growth as separate objectives. Finance can reconcile reported recovery with incremental margin and matched all-in cost; a rising list count or channel ROAS alone does not establish profit.</p>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Recart Shopify FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
